{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 10.0% a year from $129 billion in FY2017 to $303 billion in FY2026 [F1][F10][F203], with operating income growing faster at 12.3% [F204] and net income at 14.7% [F205]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The window is not a straight line: growth stepped up to 17.5% in FY2021 [D189] and 15.8% in FY2022 [D238], then fell back to 6.8% in FY2023 [D287] and 5.0% in FY2024 [D336] before recovering to 8.2% in FY2025 [D385] and 10.1% in FY2026 [D434]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2021 step came from comparable sales up 16%, with non-foods and e-commerce particularly strong, plus gasoline price and volume effects [P56][P54]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2022 peak was driven by comparable sales up 14% and a $14.8 billion increase in warehouse ancillary and other businesses, strongest in gasoline, business centers and travel, with inflation explicitly cited [P42]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2023 slowdown followed as comparable sales growth eased to 3% and non-foods sales declined [P32]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The U.S. segment supplied 72.5% of FY2026 revenue [D670] and 7.2pp of the 10.1% growth [D672], with Other International adding 1.6pp [D679] and Canada 1.3pp [D686]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2026 net sales rose $27.3 billion, or 10%, primarily on comparable sales up 8% (5% average ticket, 3% frequency) plus 25 net new warehouses [P14]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "By product, Food and Sundries contributed 2.6pp of FY2026 growth [D560] and Non-Foods 2.2pp [D576], while warehouse ancillary and other businesses jumped 19.9% for 3.7pp [D600][D601]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Membership fees grew 11.0% to $5.9 billion [D664][S78], driven by new sign-ups, fee increases and Executive upgrades, with renewal rates of 92.3% in the U.S. and Canada and 89.8% worldwide [P13]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew 12.5% against revenue growth of 10.1% in FY2026 [D435][D434], an incremental operating margin of 4.7% [D457], so profit grew faster than revenue."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS grew 14.0% against net income growth of 13.9% [D438][D436], with the diluted share count essentially flat at 444.4 million [X100][D452]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin reached 3.9% in FY2026 [F32], its window high [D691] and above the 3.4% median [D692], versus a low of 3.1% in FY2019 [D690]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The FY2026 margin rose 0.1pp [D447], with SG&A adding 0.1pp [D460] and cost of revenue flat [D459]; SG&A fell to 9.0% of revenue [D414]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "SG&A as a percentage of net sales decreased 10 basis points, though excluding gasoline price inflation it rose one basis point, and foreign currency increased SG&A by $126 [P9]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Gross margin percentage decreased three basis points, but excluding gasoline price inflation it was 11.22%, up 10 basis points, helped by IEEPA tariff refunds of three basis points [P12]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net margin reached 3.0% [F52], above the 2.6% window median [D695], with the effective tax rate at 24.7% [D420] versus 32.8% in FY2017 [D8]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow reached $15.8 billion in FY2026 [F82], 1.71x net income [D421], and free cash flow was $9.4 billion [F102], 1.02x net income [D422] against a 0.99x window median [D701]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2026 operating cash flow increase was primarily due to higher operating income and reduced net investment in merchandise inventories from faster turns and improved supplier payment terms [P6]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow margin was 3.1% [D418], above the 2.8% median [D698], while capex of $6.4 billion [F92] was 2.1% of revenue [D417] and 2.41x D&A [D423]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Investing cash outflow rose to $6.4 billion from $5.3 billion, primarily capital expenditures [P5][F112][F111]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net cash reached $15.1 billion in FY2026 [D427], 5.0% of revenue [D428], the 100th percentile against retail peers (n=6) whose median is -4.4% [D715][D716]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Cash and investments grew 39.4% to $21.3 billion [D453][D425] while total debt rose 6.5% to $6.2 billion [D454][D426], and the current ratio was 1.06x [F182] against a 1.02x median [D704]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Financing outflow of $3.4 billion covered dividends, buybacks, debt repayment and withholding taxes [P4][F122]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks plus dividends of $3.3 billion were 35.2% of free cash flow [D429][D430], and the diluted share count fell 0.1% [D452], so capital return has not shrunk the share base."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Return on average equity was 28.4% [D433], the 60th percentile against retail peers (n=5) whose median is 24.0% [D719][D720]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "No red-flag candidates were supplied in the pack, so severity and persistence cannot be ranked; the conditions screened were margin compression, cash conversion, leverage and dilution, and none of those triggered on the cited figures."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The one structural soft spot is margin level rather than direction: operating margin of 3.9% [F32] sits at the 17th percentile against retail peers (n=6) whose median is 5.0% [D709][D710], and net margin of 3.0% [F52] is also 17th percentile against a 3.5% median [D711][D712]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "That gap reflects the membership-fee model rather than deterioration, since the margin has risen from 3.1% in FY2019 [D690] to its window high [D691], but it leaves little room if merchandise costs outrun sales."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Cash conversion is the second item to watch: free cash flow/net income of 1.02x [D422] is above the 0.83x peer median [D718] but below the 1.58x window high [D700], and FY2022 showed it can fall to 0.60x [D699]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin: a FY2027 print below the 3.9% FY2026 level [F32] would reverse the trend of the last three years, while holding at or above it confirms the operating leverage; it appears in the FY2027 10-K."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow/net income: a reading below the 0.99x window median [D701] would signal working-capital or capex pressure, given FY2026's 1.02x [D422]; it appears in the FY2027 cash flow statement."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Membership fee growth: a print below the 11.0% FY2026 rate [D664] would test the fee-increase and Executive-upgrade driver cited in the filing [P13]; it appears in the FY2027 10-K."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net cash: a fall below the $9.5 billion FY2025 level [D378] from FY2026's $15.1 billion [D427] would mark a shift in capital allocation; it appears in the FY2027 balance sheet."}
  ]}
]}
